Subject: [PATCH 1/9] geph5-app: widen the libc target cfg to cover Android

On Android geph5-app links against the NDK libc, exactly as on Linux. Without
this the crate compiles for target_os="android" but every `libc::` call in
platform.rs resolves to nothing, so the Android build of geph5-app fails.

This is a single line in a dependency table, which is the least fragile place
in the whole series: nothing about it can drift out of date when upstream
refactors code around it. If this patch ever conflicts, something structural
happened to the workspace and you should re-read this file rather than force it.

---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/binaries/geph5-app/Cargo.toml b/binaries/geph5-app/Cargo.toml
index 2a2a3be..23136f9 100644
--- a/binaries/geph5-app/Cargo.toml
+++ b/binaries/geph5-app/Cargo.toml
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ tracing = "0.1.44"
 tracing-subscriber = { version = "0.3.23", features = ["json", "env-filter"] }
 url = "2"
 
-[target.'cfg(any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "macos"))'.dependencies]
+[target.'cfg(any(target_os = "linux", target_os = "android", target_os = "macos"))'.dependencies]
 libc = "0.2"
 
 [target.'cfg(target_os = "macos")'.dependencies]
